<!--
  Champion spawn definitions (Scripts/Engines/ChampionSpawn/ChampDefinitions.cs).
  Generated 10/27/26 from ChampLevelData.CreateSpawn() (r1145) and verified level-for-level against it before that code was removed.

  <Champ name="...">         a definition; a champ engine selects it by name ([props DefinitionName). Names C# relies on are in ChampNames.
    <Level ...>              one level, in order; the last level is the champion
      repeat                 optional: the level is used this many times in a row (default 1)
      maxKills               kills to advance
      maxMobs                mobiles alive at once
      maxSpawn               mobiles created per respawn
      maxRange               spawn distance from the engine
      spawnDelaySeconds      optional: delay between respawns (default 0)
      expireMinutes          time before a level that stalls drops back
      flags                  optional: SpawnFlags names, comma separated (SpawnFar, AvoidPlayers, ...)
      captain                optional: one of these per level
      <Monster type="..."/>  a mobile type; one is picked at random per spawn (list a type twice to weight it)
      <Name name="..." title="..."/>  optional: the spawned mobile is given one of these names (title optional)

  A number is a literal or a reference to a public static field of an approved class, read when the definition is
  applied to a champ (approved: CoreAI), e.g. maxKills="CoreAI.SpiritFirstWaveNumber".
  A placed champ keeps the levels it was given: a change here reaches it only when its DefinitionName is set again.
  [ChampDefs lists the definitions; [ChampDefs reload reads this file again.
-->
